<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    Bead nexus-5r2sc.2.1 (RDR-235 E1, delayed visibility on tuples).

    nexus.tuples.available_at TIMESTAMPTZ NULL: the instant from which the row may be
    claimed. NULL means "claimable now" (the claim predicate's pre-E1 behaviour); a
    non-NULL value in the future hides the row from the claim, and from the rd/in
    claimable mirrors, until the DATABASE clock reaches it. It is stamped on the database
    clock (now() + delay) by out (delay_s) and by nack (retry_after_s), the way RDR-163
    stamps next_retry_at, and cleared wherever claim_id is cleared (release, a nack without
    retry_after_s, a lapse reclaimed or dead-lettered). A dead-letter outcome leaves it NULL.

    No index (RDR-235 finding F26 / assumption A1): the claim loop already narrows on the
    subspace scan index and the filter is one more cheap arm, so an index on available_at
    would only add write cost.

    NULL is the true prior state of every existing row. There is no backfill.

    ADD COLUMN only (no UPDATE, no ALTER ... TYPE ... USING), so there is no DATA
    EFFECT line, matching tuples-009-claimed-at.xml: scripts/data_effect_lint.py's own
    scope excludes ADD COLUMN. DDL is unaffected by FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY on
    nexus.tuples.

    Placed after tuples-009-claimed-at.xml and before the grants-nexus-svc.xml runAlways
    block (the established late-append convention, D0.1).
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <changeSet id="tuples-010-1" author="nexus-5r2sc.2.1">
        <comment>Adds nexus.tuples.available_at TIMESTAMPTZ NULL -- an additive column only (ADD COLUMN, no data mutation of any existing row), so no DATA EFFECT line applies per scripts/data_effect_lint.py's own scope. NULL is the true prior state of every existing row. Stamped on the database clock by TupleRepository.out (delay_s) and nack (retry_after_s), read by the claim predicate, cleared with claim_id.</comment>
        <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">
ALTER TABLE nexus.tuples
    ADD COLUMN available_at TIMESTAMPTZ NULL;
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            <sql splitStatements="true">
                ALTER TABLE nexus.tuples DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS available_at;
            </sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
